import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About" description="About Naman, the things he keeps building, and what usually sends him down a new rabbit hole.">
  <div class="editorial-page about-editorial">
    <section class="page-hero shell shell--wide" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <p class="page-kicker">About / personal internet</p>
      <h1 id="about-title">I like turning small ideas into <span class="accent-blue">real things.</span></h1>
      <p class="page-lede">I’m Naman. Most of what I know came from getting curious, building a version, breaking something, and staying with it long enough to understand what actually matters.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-layout shell shell--wide" aria-label="About Naman">
      <div class="about-story">
        <section>
          <p class="section-kicker">01 / THE PATTERN</p>
          <h2>Build first. Figure out the edges on the way.</h2>
          <p>That is basically how this site, Get Random Letter, and most of my experiments started. I’m not following some grand roadmap. I find something interesting or annoying, build a version, test it, improve it, and write down what I learned.</p>
          <p>I like useful things, clear interfaces, weird little ideas, and the final ten percent that makes something feel finished instead of merely functional.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="exploring">
          <p class="section-kicker">02 / WHAT PULLS ME IN</p>
          <h2>Search, products, tools, and the systems between them.</h2>
          <p>SEO is a big part of my work: technical fixes, content, search data, and figuring out why a useful page isn’t getting found. Building products pulled me deeper into web development, Android, automation, AI-assisted workflows, QA, and the less glamorous details that turn an idea into something somebody else can actually use.</p>
          <p>I’m much more interested in using tools to make something useful than arguing about which tool won the week. Most of what I write comes from work I’m doing right now, including the parts I’m still figuring out.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="off-screen">
          <p class="section-kicker">03 / OFF SCREEN</p>
          <h2>A little ambition, a little chaos, plenty of chai.</h2>
          <p><em>One Piece</em> is the permanent favorite. I like stories with ridiculous ambition, strange crews, and a world that keeps getting bigger the farther you go. Chai also helps with the parts of building that somehow become 2 AM problems.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <p class="section-kicker">04 / WHY THIS SITE EXISTS</p>
          <h2>I don’t want everything I make to disappear into a feed.</h2>
          <p>I want one place where an Android utility can sit next to an open-source SEO tool, a weird browser experiment, an unfinished idea, and a post I still like six months later.</p>
          <p>Naman.blog is built with <a href="https://astro.build/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Astro</a>, mostly plain CSS, and a small amount of JavaScript. <a href="https://pages.github.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Pages</a> hosts it. The setup stays intentionally boring so the things on the site can be less boring.</p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <aside class="about-now" aria-label="A few current coordinates">
        <div class="about-now__top"><span>currently active</span><span>●</span></div>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Making</dt><dd>Products, tools, and experiments</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Working on</dt><dd>SEO + search projects</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Writing</dt><dd>What I learn while doing it</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Recharging</dt><dd>One Piece + chai</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>